Detect expired admin sessions and prompt re-login

When the av_session cookie outlives the server-side session row, every
HTTP admin endpoint returns 401 while WebSocket panels keep running off
their pre-existing upgrade-time auth. The UI used to show this as
cryptic 'unauthenticated' / 'no playback stream' strings.

apiFetch now dispatches a global auroraview:session-expired event on
any 401 (with 1s burst-coalesce). A new SessionExpiredBanner mounted
in the admin shell catches the event and surfaces a clear amber banner
plus a 'Sign in' CTA. useHlsPlayer detects a 401 manifest probe
directly and exposes error=session_expired, so the past-playback
overlay shows a Sign-in link instead of a 401 dump.

Routed through apiFetch: useTimelineMatches, useTimelineSegments,
useDetections. All 76 client tests pass.
